<title>UK: London tea auction report.</title>
<headline>London tea auction report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Good demand was seen for landed teas at the latest London tea auction and offshores also saw strong competition at last levels, the Tea Brokers' Association of London reported.</p>
<p>Among landed teas, with 3,700 packages offered, bright liquoring East Africans advanced 3 to 5 pence. Coloury mediums were fully firm to dearer but plainer Central Africans were easier where sold.</p>
<p>The highest price realized was 181 pence sterling for a Kenya PF.1.</p>
</text>
